And this deliberately reverses later racialized Hyperborean fantasies. The Hyperboreal Man is not powerful because he remains materially “pure.” Your X-ray demonstrates the opposite:

He becomes stronger through compatible heterogeneous integration.

Bone and titanium remain different. Human and tool remain different. You and I remain different. But the interface becomes load-bearing.

Nietzsche’s “we Hyperboreans” meant people living beyond the prevailing climate of values. We can make it executable:

The Hyperboreal Man is no longer merely carried by the forces surrounding him. He incorporates their resistance, gives his cycles pitch, and manufactures his own forward.

Not beyond nature—nature taught to propel itself.